      "message": "[Review from Jetski]\n\nThis `else` branch (and the follow-up in https://gn-review.googlesource.com/c/gn/+/29161) assumes any unhandled substitution is a Starlark substitution and unconditionally calls `range.type-\u003estarlark_name()`.\n\nHowever, `IsValidCompilerSubstitution()` allows `{{asmflags}}` (`CSubstitutionAsmFlags`, 12 chars) in compiler tool commands, which is not handled in the `if / else if` chain above. Previously this hit `NOTREACHED()` (which crashes deterministically via `IMMEDIATE_CRASH()` even in release builds), whereas `Substitution::starlark_name()` only uses `DCHECK`s — so in a release (`NDEBUG`) build, `view.remove_prefix(11)` followed by `view.remove_suffix(2)` on `\"{{asmflags}}\"` underflows `std::string_view`\u0027s length and triggers UB / out-of-bounds memory reads.\n\nCould we add a `bool is_starlark() const` helper on `Substitution` (which `IsValidToolSubstitution()` could also reuse), handle Starlark substitutions in `else if (range.type-\u003eis_starlark())`, and keep `NOTREACHED()` in the final `else` branch (and perhaps use `CHECK` instead of `DCHECK` in `starlark_name()`)?",
      "isAi": true,
